referenceFunction.generalComment:
Solar-grade silicon (about 99.9999999% = 9N purity) is mainly produced by the modified Siemens process. The share of solar-grade silicon produced in fluidised bed reactors (FBR) is <5% according to ITRPV 2020. This production route is not modelled separately because life cycle inventory data are not available. The share of electronic-grade and electronic off-grade silicon used in the PV industry is considered negligible. Imports of polysilicon are not taken into account since domestic production of polysilicon is sufficient to cover wafer production.;
CAS number: 7440-21-3; 
Formula: Si; 
UUID: 51f463ee-66c0-396d-ad97-0023f642fce9
